GitOps-Based Kubernetes Deployment
with Argo CD
Project Documentation & Interview Reference Guide
DevOps Portfolio Project  |  CI/CD & GitOps Automation

1. Project Overview
This project demonstrates a complete GitOps workflow for deploying and managing applications on Kubernetes using Argo CD. The Git repository acts as the single source of truth for the desired state of the cluster, and Argo CD continuously reconciles the live cluster state against that source, enabling automated, auditable, and self-healing deployments.
Objectives
•	Implement automated synchronization between Git and Kubernetes
•	Demonstrate configuration drift detection and self-healing
•	Perform Git-based rollback for failed or unwanted changes
•	Establish a clean separation between Continuous Integration (Jenkins) and Continuous Deployment (Argo CD)
2. Architecture
The end-to-end pipeline follows this flow:
Developer  →  GitHub  →  Jenkins (CI)  →  Amazon ECR  →  GitOps Repo  →  Argo CD  →  Kubernetes
Jenkins is responsible for the CI stage — building, testing, scanning, and pushing container images to Amazon ECR. Once a new image is ready, the GitOps repository is updated with the new image tag, and Argo CD takes over the CD stage, syncing the declared state from Git into the Kubernetes cluster.
