10. Interview Talking Points
Suggested points to highlight when presenting this project to an interviewer:
1.	Explain "why GitOps" — Git as the single source of truth, full auditability via commit history, and easy rollback compared to imperative kubectl deployments.
2.	Walk through the architecture diagram: Developer → GitHub → Jenkins (CI) → ECR → GitOps repo → Argo CD → Kubernetes.
3.	Describe the CI/CD separation — Jenkins never touches the cluster directly, only Argo CD does, which reduces the attack surface and enforces Git as the gatekeeper.
4.	Demonstrate understanding of reconciliation loops — Automated Sync, Self-Heal, and Prune — and what each one solves operationally.
5.	Give a concrete example of drift detection and self-healing (manual scale-down being auto-corrected back to the Git-declared replica count).
6.	Explain rollback as a simple git revert rather than a manual kubectl rollout undo, and why that's more auditable.
7.	Mention the Argo CD components (API Server, Repo Server, Application Controller, Redis) to show depth beyond just using the UI.

